      "message": "The old code would first add the dev map entry, then set the limit, and then create the rule. Maybe we can keep the same order here, and only add the rule after maybeAddDevMap and maybeSetLimit? That way we know that BPF won\u0027t forward anything until the limit is set, and we\u0027ll have fewer NO_LIMIT_ENTRY errors.\n\n    maybeAddDevMap(...);\n    maybeSetLimit(...);\n    if (!mBpfCoordinatorShim.addIpv6UpstreamRule(rule)) {\n        return;\n    }\n    ArraySet\u003cIpv6UpstreamRule\u003e rules \u003d mIpv6UpstreamRules.computeIfAbsent(\n            ipServer, k -\u003e new ArraySet\u003cIpv6UpstreamRule\u003e());\n    rules.add(rule);",
